fn from_text(s: str) -> bytes
    The UTF-8 encoding of s; from_text("") is the empty bytes value.
fn to_text(b: bytes) -> result[str]
    b as text when it is well-formed UTF-8; else err("not UTF-8 at byte N").
fn from_ints(xs: list[int]) -> bytes
    Bytes from integers 0 to 255; another value stops the program with R0007 naming its index.
fn to_ints(b: bytes) -> list[int]
    The bytes as integers 0 to 255.
fn to_hex(b: bytes) -> str
    Two lowercase hex digits per byte.
fn from_hex(s: str) -> result[bytes]
    Bytes from hex digits (either case); err("invalid hex: S; not hex at position N") or err("invalid hex: S; odd number of hex digits").
fn to_base64(b: bytes) -> str
    Base64 (RFC 4648, standard alphabet, padded).
fn from_base64(s: str) -> result[bytes]
    Bytes from padded standard base64; err("invalid base64: S; not base64 at position N") or err("invalid base64: S; length is not a multiple of 4").
fn read_stdin() -> bytes uses input
    All of standard input, as bytes (any bytes; read_all and read_line need UTF-8).
fn write_stdout(b: bytes) uses console
    Writes b to standard output as it is, with no newline.
